# A real Get-Printer-Attributes reply, captured rather than written by hand.
#
# Captured  2026-08-24 from an HP Color LaserJet MFP M283fdw (the printer this
#           proxy was built for; it answers Get-Printer-Attributes as
#           "HP ColorLaserJet MFP M282-M285"), by sending operation 0x000B with
#           requested-attributes = all to ipp://PRINTER/ipp/print and storing
#           the response body verbatim. 12453 bytes, 130 printer attributes.
#
# Why captured: an attribute set written by hand drifts away from what real
# firmware sends -- the number of attributes, their order, their tags, the
# collections and the multi-values -- and a test built on it then passes while
# describing a printer that does not exist. This is the bytes off the wire.
#
# Sanitised, and ONLY this. Four values carried device- or site-specific
# identifiers. Each was replaced by a placeholder of exactly the same length,
# so the message is still byte-exact and every value length still matches its
# value:
#
#     the printer's address -> 192.0.2.10    (7x; house rule: no real network
#                                             detail in the tree, and RFC 5737
#                                             is the range reserved for that)
#     printer-name          -> NPI000000     (HP derives it from the MAC)
#     printer-dns-sd-name   -> ...(000000)   (likewise)
#     printer-uuid          -> ...0000000000 (the MAC once more)
#
# What was replaced is named; what it was replaced with is shown; what it used
# to be is deliberately absent. Recording the pre-images here would undo the
# work -- a reader holding both the before and the after has back the very
# value the substitution existed to remove. For the same reason the check in
# scripts/selftest.sh looks for anything SHAPED like an address or a MAC,
# instead of comparing against the originals.
#
# Nothing else was touched: no attribute was added, removed, reordered or
# retyped. serialize(parse(x)) == x holds, and scripts/selftest.sh asserts it.
#
# Base64 of the raw IPP response body follows.
